PART H – EC2 CLEANUP AND COST CONTROL

24. STOP AND RESTART KAFKA CONTAINER

After the training, stop the container if you want to pause the Kafka process.

Stop Kafka:

```bash
sudo docker stop kafka-day1
```

Restart Kafka:

```bash
sudo docker start kafka-day1
```

Check container status:

```bash
sudo docker ps
```

Important:

For this classroom configuration, Kafka's data resides in the container's writable storage.

Removing and recreating the container can lose the lab data.

For subsequent days, use persistent Docker volumes before relying on the environment for important work.

25. AWS EC2 COST MANAGEMENT

Stop the EC2 instance from the AWS Console when it is not required.

Important:

EBS storage and some public IPv4 allocations can still incur charges even when the EC2 instance is stopped.

Terminate the instance and delete unneeded resources when the training environment is no longer required.

